+### 0.2 Assumptions (A1–A6)
+
+- **A1.** `VICHE_STATE_ROOT=/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche-state`, `VICHE_TOWN_ROOT=/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche` (verified via env and script defaults).
+- **A2.** `suite-compliance-check.sh` is read-only (verified by reading: only `git` read commands + state file reads; no writes).
+- **A3.** The sole writer of `suite-compliance-*.json` is `government/judiciary-measurements.py::suite_compliance()` (grep-verified; the only other references are the checker itself and `LAWS.md`).
+- **A4.** "Status distribution (measured/unreadable/red_chronology_unresolved/other)" = snapshot `summary.status` ∈ {measured, other} plus `per_change.status` ∈ {unreadable, compliant, red_chronology_unresolved, violation, other}.
+- **A5.** Driver classification by commit-message prefix is a heuristic; commits with generic messages (e.g. `Merge origin/main`) are bucketed as legacy.
+- **A6.** Aggregate snapshot-row counts overcount distinct commits (a commit appears in every snapshot after it lands); distinct-commit measures are reported separately.
+
+### 0.3 Limits
+
+- Single measurement point (2026-11-23); counts drift as `main` grows (~1 snapshot per ~221 s).
+- No compliance verdicts; no grading of individual officers or seats. Commits are classified by message prefix and date, never by author blame.
+- **"Axon branches"**: I could not locate a separately named "Axon" surface. I treated `viche-state` as the instrumented Viche-state surface and the town repo (`viche`) as the commit/evidence surface. Seat worktrees under `viche-seats/branches/` (230 branches) contain no suite-compliance instruments of their own; instrumentation is centralized. If "Axon" denotes a distinct surface, this report does not cover it — flagged as a gap (see §2.4).
+- The full per-file table is embedded in Appendix A; the raw measurement TSV is at `/tmp/opencode/state/coverage-per-file.tsv`.
